[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m ### **Step 2: Compute and Factorize 9!**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m The value of $9!$ is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m 9! = 362880
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m We factor $9!$ into its prime factors:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m 9! = 2^7 \cdot 3^4 \cdot 5^1 \cdot 7^1
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m ### **Step 3: Determine What Divisors Are Relevant**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m To have a units digit of 1, the number must end in 1. That means:
