[36m(TaskRunner pid=498088)[0m - Since 5 is a prime factor, if a number has a factor of 5, its units digit would be 0, 5, or something else. Check: $d \equiv 1 \pmod{10}$, so any divisor divisible by 5 cannot end in 1. Therefore, no such divisors can have 5 as a factor.
